\ul\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 expertise defense}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 : if one has expert knowledge about some philosophical issue (e.g., the free will debate) the in\u-1278\'3f
uences of extraneous features (e.g., personality) would not matter or would be dramatically reduced.
\par Intuitive judgments are prima facie better because the non-intuitive theories should provide an error theory for why folk thinks differently.
\par NEO-PI-R: each personality factor is itemized into 6 facets. Facets of extraversion: warmth, gregariousness, assertiveness, activity, excitement seeking, and positive emotion.
\par The }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \ul\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 experiment}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 : 10 questions about the free-will debate to discriminate between experts and non-experts. }{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \ul\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 Hypotheses}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 : \bullet  extraversion will predict compatibilist judgments. \bullet  Experts will be more incom}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486 patibi}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 lists than non-experts. \bullet 
 Extraversion will continue to predict judgment biases in experts. Also checked for the Need for Cognition.
\par The story: Most respected neuroscientists [\'85] speci\u-1279\'3fc chemical reactions and neural processes occurring in our brains. [\'85] John decides to kill a shop owner because he needs money and does it. Once the speci\u-1279\'3f
c thoughts, desires, and plans occur in John\rquote s mind, they will de\u-1279\'3fnitely cause his decision to kill a shop owner. Chemical reactions and neural processes in the story mixed with mind, thoughts}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid1068486 ,}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486  and desires in the actual case. The questions: 1 (absolutely agree)\emdash 7 (absolutely disagree): \bullet  John is morally responsible for his action. \bullet 
 John did it because of his own free will. \bullet  John\rquote s decision was up to him.
\par Results: \bullet  Warmth was the only facet related to compatibilistic judgments in a simple regression, 6% of the variance. \bullet  Greater philosophical knowledge was associated with more incompatibilist intuitions. The cognitive re\u-1278\'3f
ection task was not reliably related to intuitions in this scenario. \bullet  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \ul\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 Among experts, warmth continued to predict a moderate amount of unique judgment variance}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486  (about 5% of variance).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \ul\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 Interpretation}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 : }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486 Personality differences}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486  are heritable, and thus differences in philosophical views might be heritable as well. Three different ways for genotype and environment to covary. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 Active}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 : one chooses environments according to one\rquote s genes. For example, each new generation of philosophers, because of their personality, \u-1279
\'3fnds some positions and examples intuitively appealing and adopts them. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \i\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 Reactive}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 : where one\rquote 
s reaction to an environment is partially in\u-1278\'3fuenced by one\rquote s genes. For example, each new gen
eration of philosophers will likely adopt a view that is consistent with previous philosophers with similar personalities because they react positively to views that are the same as their own. }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 
\i\insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 Passive}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af31507 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1068486\charrsid1068486 : where one\rquote 
s environment is mostly formed by people that share in part the same genes. For example, if one is the child of a philosopher, one will probably not only share half of one\rquote s genes, but also some philosophy books.
\par Personality biases can lead to errors but also better accuracy. It is not clear why extraverts\rquote  intuitions should be trusted in Neo-Platonic projects, though it may be desirable for a jury to consist partially or completely of extraverts.\cell 
